// core/scene/include/CAD_0/scene/scene.hpp
//
// Scene — a collection of named nodes with transforms. Three kinds of
// node (ADR-0002 honest dispatch — a node is ONE thing, never a fake
// other thing):
//
//   * Sdf   — parametric/analytic body (SDFBody) + optional shape factory
//             for interactive editing; the display mesh is a tessellation
//             CACHE regenerated by update_meshes(). An OPERATION node
//             (recipe set) is an Sdf node whose provenance explains the
//             body (Phase F / ADR-0030 D2).
//   * Mesh  — imported geometry (TriangleMesh) as a first-class payload;
//             there is no body to evaluate, no builder/params/factory, and
//             update_meshes() SKIPS the node: its "cached mesh" IS the
//             geometry (see display_mesh()).
//   * Sketch — 2D data on the world XY plane (ADR-0030 D2): entity chains,
//             NO body (nothing 3D to evaluate), NO cached mesh
//             (update_meshes() skips it by kind), NO factory. Its editing
//             surface is the entity payload; the extrude operation
//             downstream owns the 3D.

